t hurts U.S. merchants exporting)\n- Liquidity sensitivity: **\u22121**\n- Economic cycle sensitivity: **\u22122** (cross-border DTC spend is discretionary)\n- Commodity sensitivity: **0** (logistics costs, minor)\n\n**Step 1-4. Macro Alignment**\nRegime-weighted macro score = 0.25*(+2) + 0.40*(\u22121) + 0.25*(\u22121) + 0.10*(\u22122) = **\u22120.25 \u2192 Neutral-to-Headwind**.\n**Judgment:** Headwind. Conviction \u22120.5, and entry strategy is staggered rather than full-size.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 1.5-1. Base Rates [Reference, updated from framework]**\n- High-growth platform / e-commerce-enabler 5-year survival: **~50\u201360%**\n- Sustained 10-year revenue CAGR > 20% for public software/platform companies: **~20\u201330%**\n- Platform-transition success (Shopify-type partnerships converting to durable revenue): **~25\u201335%**\n- Probability that a company with one year of GAAP profitability keeps EBIT margin above 20% by year 10: **~35\u201345%**\n\n**Step 1.5-2. Deviation from Base Rate**\nMy base case embeds a 10-year revenue CAGR of ~18.3% (from $0.96B to $5.17B). This is above the ~20\u201330% base rate, so I require company-specific justification:\n1. Actual 5-year revenue CAGR of **47.8%** [Actual, SECTION 7];\n2. \"Rule of 50\" achieved in Q1 and Q2 2026 \u2014 GMV +40%/44%, revenue +33%/39%, with adjusted EBITDA margin expansion to 19.9%/20.9% [Actual, company PR];\n3. Multi-year Shopify strategic partnership renewal signed in 2026 [Estimate, web brief \u2014 company IR release exists but fetch failed], supporting a durable distribution channel.\n\n**Step 1.5-3. Base-Rate Shock Check**\nMy 10-year success probability is approximately 45\u201350%, versus ~25\u201330% base rate. This is 1.5\u20131.7x base rate \u2014 above the 1.5x threshold, requiring the additional evidence above. It is below the 2.0x red flag. **No automatic reversion to base rate, but scenario weights are tilted conservative.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY ASSESSMENT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2-1. Business Understanding**\nGlobal-E is a cross-border e-commerce localization platform. It enables DTC merchants to sell internationally by handling local currency conversion, duty/tax calculation and collection, fraud prevention, shipping, and compliance. It serves both direct merchants and large platforms, most notably Shopify Markets Pro. Revenue is a blend of service fees and fulfillment fees. **Understandability: High.**\n\n**Step 2-2. Moat Assessment**\n| Moat Type | Score (0\u20133) | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand, regulatory license network) | 2 | Stable |\n| Switching costs (merchant integration, data history) | 3 | Widening |\n| Network effects (merchants \u2194 logistics \u2194 local tax/jurisdiction) | 2 | Widening |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Stable |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening |\n| Regulatory barriers (local tax/duty apparatus) | 2 | Stable |\n| Data moat | 2 | Widening |\n| **Total** | **14/21** | **Wide Moat, Stable-to-Widening** |\n\nKey signal: Shopify renewed on a multi-year basis [Estimate], and GMV growth accelerated to 44% in Q2 2026 [Actual].\n\n**Step 2-3. Lynch Classification**\n**Fast Grower** \u2014 revenue growth >30%, gross margin 45%, now GAAP profitable. Checkpoints: must maintain growth without debt; dilution must stay controlled; competition risk is higher than for Stalwarts.\n\n**Step 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard**\n- Revenue 5-yr CAGR: **47.8%** [Actual, SECTION 7]\n- FY2025 revenue: **$0.962B** [Actual]\n- Gross margin FY2025: **45.3%** [Actual]\n- GAAP operating margin FY2025: **+7.4%** [Actual]\n- Net margin FY2025: **+7.1%** [Actual]\n- FCF (OCF \u2212 capex): **$0.281B** [Actual]; SBC: **$0.039B** [Actual]\n- Net cash: ~$0.449B cash + ST investments less lease liabilities [Estimate]\n- ROIC: approx **12%** (NOPAT ~$61M / invested capital ~$508M) [Estimate]\n**Judgment: Good.**\n\n**Step 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard**\n1. Buyback efficiency: 1/3 \u2014 announced $500M repurchase, pending Israeli regulatory approval [Estimate], no history.\n2. M&A track record: 2/3 \u2014 Passport acquisition closed July 2026; integration yet to prove.\n3. Capex efficiency: 2/3 \u2014 capex only 0.3% of revenue, high incremental ROIC.\n4. Rationality of mix: 2/3 \u2014 using stock + cash for acquisition is reasonable.\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3/3 \u2014 Q1/Q2 2026 beat and FY guidance was raised twice [Actual/PR].\n- Insider ownership: 30.53% [Aggregator] \u2192 +1 bonus.\n**Total: 11/15 + 1 = 12/16. Good.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2.5-1/2. SBC and Economic FCF**\n- FY2025 SBC = **$39M** [Actual] = 4.1% of revenue. This is a real expense; adjusted FCF = reported FCF minus SBC = $281M \u2212 $39M = **$242M** [Arithmetic].\n- However, reported OCF of $284M was boosted by a large working-capital build (merchant payables / deferred revenue). My DCF uses EBIT-based FCF, which excludes this benefit, a more conservative treatment.\n\n**Step 2.5-3. Operating Leases**\nOperating leases = **$24M** [Actual, SECTION 6B]. No long-term debt [Actual]. Net cash after Passport cash consideration ~ **$200M** [Estimate].\n\n**Step 2.5-4. R&D Capitalization**\nR&D is not separately disclosed in the pack [Unconfirmed]; no adjustment made.\n\n**Step 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC**\nAdjusted ROIC = NOPAT / (equity + leases + debt \u2212 cash) \u2248 $61M / ($933M + $24M \u2212 $449M) \u2248 **12%** [Estimate]. Gap vs GAAP ROIC (~17% vendor) is due to xero cash balance treatment; no 5pt gap requiring adjustment.\n\n**Step 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett-style)**\nFY2025 Owner Earnings \u2248 Net income + D&A \u2212 maintenance capex \u2212 non-cash working capital expansion (excl. cash) = $68M + $2M \u2212 $3M \u2212 (\u2212$147M) = **$214M** [Estimate]. This benefits from growing merchant float; use cautiously.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 3-1. Discount-Rate Derivation**\n- Risk-free rate (10Y UST): **4.71%** [Actual, FRED 2026-08-21]\n- Equity beta: **1.011** [Aggregator, window unverified]\n- Equity risk premium: **4.5%** [Assumption, Damodaran-style]\n- Cost of equity = 4.71% + 1.011 \u00d7 4.5% = **9.26%**\n- Small-cap / emerging-platform premium: **+0.25%** [Assumption]\n- **WACC = 9.5%** (no debt; effective WACC = cost of equity)\n\n**Step 3-2. Revenue Forecast (Base Case)**\n| FY | Revenue ($M) | Growth | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2025 | 962 | actual | [Actual] |\n| 2026E | 1,330 | +38.3% | Company guidance midpoint [Actual] |\n| 2027E | 1,696 | +27.5% | Consensus forward growth [Estimate, yfinance] |\n| 2028E | 2,077 | +22.5% | [Assumption] fade |\n| 2029E | 2,493 | +20.0% | [Assumption] fade |\n| 2030E | 2,943 | +18.0% | [Assumption] fade |\n| 2031E | 3,415 | +16.0% | [Assumption] fade |\n| 2032E | 3,889 | +14.0% | [Assumption] fade |\n| 2033E | 4,356 | +12.0% | [Assumption] fade |\n| 2034E | 4,791 | +10.0% | [Assumption] fade |\n| 2035E | 5,174 | +8.0% | [Assumption] fade to terminal |\n| Terminal | \u2014 | 3.0% | [Assumption] 3% \u2264 long-run nominal GDP |\n\n**Step 3-3. Margin and FCF Forecast (Base Case)**\n- GAAP EBIT margin: FY2026E **10.5%** \u2192 FY2035E **22.0%** [Assumption]. Rationale: 2026 adjusted EBITDA margin \u2248 21% [Actual PR], less 4.5% SBC [Assumption] and other non-cash/excluded items; long-term adjusted EBITDA margin ~25\u201326%, less mature SBC ~3%, giving 22%.\n- Tax rate: **15%** [Assumption] \u2014 Israeli corporate rate modernized with NOLs/deferred assets.\n- Capex: **1.0%** of revenue [Assumption], above trailing 0.3% [Actual] to fund Passport logistics and platform.\n\n| FY | Revenue | EBIT margin | EBIT | NOPAT | Capex | FCF | PV @9.5% |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | 1,330 | 10.5% | 140 | 119 | 13 | 106 | 96 |\n| 2027E | 1,696 | 12.5% | 212 | 180 | 17 | 163 | 136 |\n| 2028E | 2,077 | 14.5% | 301 | 256 | 21 | 235 | 179 |\n| 2029E | 2,493 | 16.0% | 399 | 339 | 25 | 314 | 219 |\n| 2030E | 2,943 | 17.5% | 515 | 438 | 29 | 408 | 259 |\n| 2031E | 3,415 | 19.0% | 649 | 552 | 34 | 517 | 300 |\n| 2032E | 3,889 | 20.0% | 778 | 661 | 39 | 622 | 330 |\n| 2033E | 4,356 | 21.0% | 915 | 778 | 44 | 734 | 355 |\n| 2034E | 4,791 | 21.5% | 1,030 | 876 | 48 | 828 | 366 |\n| 2035E | 5,174 | 22.0% | 1,138 | 968 | 52 | 916 | 370 |\n\n**Terminal Value (base):**\nTV = FCF2035 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.095 \u2212 0.03) = $916M \u00d7 1.03 / 0.065 = **$14,515M**\nPV of TV = $14,515M \u00d7 0.4035 = **$5,857M**\nSum of PV of FCFs: **$2,610M**\nEnterprise value: **$8,467M**\nNet cash (incl. short-term investments, net of operating leases and Passport cash outlay): **+$200M** [Estimate]\nEquity value: **$8,667M**\nDiluted shares: **180M** [Assumption]\n**Base intrinsic value: $48.2/share**\n\n**Step 3-4. Multiples Cross-Check**\n- 2026E EV/Sales = ($8,467M / $1,330M) = **6.4x** [Estimate]\n- 2026E EV/EBIT = ($8,467M / $140M) = **60x** [Estimate]\n- FY2027E EV/Sales = 5.0x; this is comparable to high-growth platform peers (Shopify ~8\u201310x, Adyen ~15\u201320x), not expensive for 25%+ grower but not cheap.\n- Trailing P/E = 47.9x [Aggregator], consistent with high near-term margin expansion.\n\n**Step 3-5. Tornado Sensitivity (Top 3 drivers)**\n1. **Terminal EBIT margin (18\u201325%)**: IV range ~$38\u2013$58.\n2. **WACC (8.5\u201310.5%)**: IV range ~$59\u2013$40.5.\n3. **FY2027 revenue growth (20\u201335%)**: IV range ~$43\u2013$52.\nThese three variables are the Thesis KPIs for monitoring.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Competitive Response (\u22122):** Shopify, Adyen, and Stripe can build or compete with cross-border tools. The newly-renewed multi-year Shopify partnership [Estimate] mitigates near-term risk, but 2030+ competition is a live threat. If Global-E succeeds, Shopify may internalize more of the stack rather than renew at scale.\n\n**Reflexivity (Positive):** Higher stock price allows lower-dilution acquisition currency (used in Passport: half stock), attracts talent via SBC, and strengthens merchant trust. Negative reflexivity is muted given low short interest.\n\n**Customer Behavior Evolution:** Early-adopter DTC brands are moving to mainstream; the U.S. de minimis exemption ending in 2025 [Actual, Avalara/Euromonitor] raises friction for low-value cross-border parcels, pushing volume toward larger, compliance-heavy merchants \u2014 which favors Global-E's managed-market model but may cut total package volumes. Net impact: uncertain.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Prior (from base rates):** P(sustain >20% growth 10yr) \u2248 25\u201330%.\n\n**Bayesian Update:**\n- Likelihood from company-specific evidence: 2 consecutive \"Rule of 50\" quarters, renewed Shopify partnership, raised FY guidance, positive GAAP operating income \u2192 likelihood ratio ~1.6.\n- Posterior success probability \u2248 **45%** [Estimate].\n\n**Scenario Distribution (sums to 100%):**\n| Scenario | Probability | Revenue path / assumptions | IV/share |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | 30% | 2027 +25% fading to 3% by 2035; terminal EBIT margin 18%; WACC 10% | $27 |\n| Base | 50% | Table in Section 3 | $48 |\n| Bull | 20% | 2027 +32% fading to 6%; terminal EBIT margin 25%; WACC 9% | $72 |\n\nExpected value = 0.30\u00d7$27 + 0.50\u00d7$48 + 0.20\u00d7$72 = **$46.5/share**\n50% CI: **$27\u2013$72** [Estimate]\n80% CI: **$22\u2013$82** [Estimate]\n\n**Margin of Safety:**\n- vs Base IV $48.2: **15.9%** \u2014 Adequate\n- vs EV $46.5: **12.8%** \u2014 Limited\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Market-Implied Horizon:** At $40.55, market is pricing approximately 5\u20136 years of ~25% growth followed by a sharp fade to 3% [Estimate, reverse-DCF inference].\n**My Horizon:** 3\u20135 years, anchored on FY2026 guidance and FY2027 consensus.\n**Spread:** ~1\u20132 years. This is a moderate arbitrage, not extreme. Current price is roughly fair if one believes in a normal fade; upside exists only if Global-E sustains above-consensus execution.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\