 of 50\" achieved for 2 consecutive quarters,\n  adjusted EBITDA margin 20.9% [Actual].\n- A blended engine is NOT required (criteria >80% met). I apply **Engine 3: Hybrid Valuation (Product-Platform)**\n  as primary, cross-checked with **Engine 1: Traditional DCF** because GLBE's economic engine is bifurcated \u2014\n  a high-margin software/networked platform (service fees) + a lower-margin logistics stack (fulfillment services,\n  now enlarged by Passport). DCF is the anchor; segment-level multiple analysis is the cross-check.\n\n**Step 0-2 Engine Selection Rationale:**\n1. Service fees revenue (platform monetization of GMV at ~6.7% take rate [Arithmetic \u2014 $139.4M service fees / $2.089B GMV, Q2 2026]) is a classic high-gross-margin recurring platform business.\n2. Fulfillment services revenue ($159.6M in Q2 2026 [Actual]) is lower-margin, pass-through logistics; valuing the whole company at a single-platform multiple would overstate value; valuing it at logistics multiples would understate the platform.\n3. The Passport acquisition (closed 1-Jul-2026) permanently changes the revenue mix optics \u2014 $100M of ~logistics-type revenue added in CY2026 [Actual - company IR]. Segment-level accounting is essential for a defensible multiple.\n4. Reverse DCF feasibility: a pure DCF applied to the consolidated revenue line confounds two very different margin/capital-intensity profiles; Engine 3 forces separate treatment.\n\n**Layer 0-4 Key Classifications:**\n\n| Attribute | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Price (T0) | $40.55 | [Aggregator - vendor quote 2026-08-24] |\n| Basic shares outstanding (vendor) | 167,967,400 | [Aggregator] |\n| Diluted shares (my estimate) | ~177M | [Estimate] \u2014 FY25 wtd-avg 175.99M [Filed], plus Passport share consideration (~4.3M @ ~$40.55), less Q2 2026 buybacks ($68M \u2248 1.7M shares) [Actual]. |\n| Diluted market cap (T0) | \u2248 $7.18B | [Arithmetic] |\n| FY2026 revenue guidance | $1.305\u20131.355B (+38% YoY) | [Actual - company guidance 12-Aug-2026, via StockTitan] |\n| FY2026 adjusted EBITDA guidance | $278\u2013300M (~21.7% margin) | [Actual - company guidance] |\n| FY2026 GMV guidance | $8.81\u20139.11B | [Actual - company guidance] |\n| Net cash (est., post-Passport & buyback) | \u2248 +$250M | [Estimate \u2014 FY25 cash $375M + ST investments $74M \u2212 vendor total debt $24M \u2212 operating leases $24M \u2212 $175M Passport cash \u2212 $68M buyback] |\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT ANALYSIS\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n\n**Step 1-1 Macro Variable Check [T0 \u2014 Aug 2026]:**\n\n| Variable | Level | Direction | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 10-Year Treasury yield | 4.65% | \u2248 flat (vs 4.30% a year ago) | [Actual - yCharts, 24-Aug-2026] |\n| Real rates (10Y TIPS implied) | ~2.0-2.2% | Elevated | [Estimate \u2014 derived from H.15, Fed] |\n| Dollar Index (DXY) | Elevated, ~97-100 | Sideways | [Assumption \u2014 not in pack; no new data retrieved] |\n| Fed policy stance | Neutral/Hold \u2014 rates above 4%; disinflation paused | Restrictive-to-neutral | [Assumption \u2014 10Y at 4.65%, no rate-cut evidence] |\n| Economic cycle | Late expansion \u2014 growth positive, inflation ~3% | Mature | [Assumption] |\n| Credit spreads | Tight | Stable | [Assumption] |\n\n**Step 1-2 Regime Probability Distribution:**\n\n| Regime | Probability | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Reflation (High rates + Growth) | 45% | 10Y 4.65% + positive nominal GDP growth; fits current configuration best |\n| Goldilocks (Low rates + Growth) | 30% | Disinflation continues, Fed cuts later in 2026-27 |\n| Stagflation (High rates + Low growth) | 15% | Tariff shocks from trade policy; energy shocks |\n| Recession (Low rates + Low growth) | 10% | Late-cycle risk; consumer deceleration |\n| **Total** | **100%** | |\n\n**Step 1-3 Macro Sensitivity (5 axes, \u22123 to +3):**\n- Interest-rate sensitivity: **+1** (long-duration tech multiple; but net cash balance, takes no debt)\n- Dollar sensitivity: **+1** (strong USD is a tailwind for US consumers buying cross-border \u2014 GLBE's core lane; a weak USD would be a modest headwind)\n- Liquidity/risk-appetite sensitivity: **+2** (high-beta cross-border e-commerce platform; sensitive to tech multiple compression)\n- Economic-cycle sensitivity: **+2** (consumer discretionary spend via e-commerce is cyclical at the margin; e-commerce share gains offset)\n- Commodity sensitivity: **\u22121** (parcel/shipping costs matter, but fulfillment is largely pass-through)\n\n**Step 1-4 Macro Alignment: Tailwind / Neutral (net +1.0)**\n- 0.45\u00d7Reflation + 0.30\u00d7Goldilocks \u2192 a mixed but modestly supportive environment for a US-import-oriented cross-border platform. Tariff/geopolitical risk is the active macro question \u2014 a two-sided tail risk rather than a base-case driver. **Macro alignment: Neutral (+0.0 conviction adjustment).** The expansion of GLBE's e-commerce category is a structural secular growth story that overrides most cyclical sensitivity.\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 1.5. BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN CHECK\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n\n**Step 1.5-1 Similar Enterprise Base Rates:**\n- Platform/network businesses with GMV >$8B, revenue >$1B, and Rule of 50 achieved: 5-year survival rate \u2248 **70-80%** [Estimate \u2014 e-commerce enabler comps: Adyen, Checkout.com, Stripe; most achieved sustained profitability]\n- High-growth tech that reaches 20%+ adjusted EBITDA margin: probability of maintaining ROIC > WACC for 5 years \u2248 **60%** [Estimate \u2014 base rate from software comps]\n- Cross-border e-commerce enabler (GLBE category) \u2014 probability of sustaining >20% revenue growth for 5 more years \u2248 **40-50%** [Estimate \u2014 category still in early innings; e-commerce globalization <20% penetrated]\n- Platform transition success (add logistics via M&A): **30-40%** [Estimate \u2014 logistics acquisitions historically integrate poorly]\n- Large-ish M&A ($425M) achieving ROIC > WACC within 5 years: **~35%** [Base rate reference \u2014 Layer 1.5]\n\n**Step 1.5-2 Deviation from Base Rate \u2014 requires 3+ specific justifications:**\n1. **Repeated upward guidance revisions** \u2014 Q2 2026 raised FY26 revenue by ~$80M at the midpoint; the company has now raised guidance twice in the last 2 quarters [Actual]. This is unusually strong execution evidence vs. peers.\n2. **Metric-level discipline** \u2014 Management publishes an Excel KPI file and reports Rule of 50 quarterly; GMV, take rate, service-fee revenue and adjusted EBITDA are all disclosed, reducing the information asymmetry that drives base-rate failure.\n3. **Shopify partnership durability** \u2014 the deepest distribution relationship in cross-border e-commerce (Shopify Managed Markets) with visible 2.0 expansion and multi-year merchant onboarding cohorts [Actual - company press release]. This lowers customer-acquisition risk relative to the typical standalone platform.\n\u2192 Net assessment: with success probability ~65% vs. category base rate ~50%, we are +30% above base. Below the 1.5\u00d7 threshold; no automatic red flag. No 2.0\u00d7 shock.\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY ASSESSMENT\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n\n**Step 2-1 Business Understanding (3 sentences):**\n1. GLBE is a cross-border e-commerce enablement platform that lets global merchants \"go global\" by localizing checkout, currency, duties, taxes, shipping and returns in over 100 markets \u2014 converting international visitors into customers.\n2. It earns a service fee (~6.7% of GMV [Estimate \u2014 2026]) for the software/networked platform and a fulfillment fee for handling physical cross-border logistics/duties/returns.\n3. Its distribution moat is anchored by deep platform partnerships (primarily Shopify Managed Markets) and is now augmented by the Passport logistics acquisition (closed 1-Jul-2026, $350M + up to $75M contingent [Actual]).\nUnderstandability: **High**.\n\n**Step 2-2 Moat Assessment + Moat Dynamics:**\n\n| Moat Type | Score (0-3) | Direction | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand) | 1 | Stable | Not a consumer brand, but trusted enterprise vendor |\n| Switching costs | 3 | Widening | Multi-year integrations into merchant stacks; Managed Markets embeds GLBE deeper |\n| Network effects | 2 | Widening | Cross-border scale \u2192 better carrier/duty data \u2192 better pricing \u2192 more merchants; two-sided value improving |\n| Cost advantage | 2 | Stable | Passport adds US domestic logistics scale [Actual]; AI efficiency gains quoted by mgmt [Actual] |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening | 300 bps EBITDA margin expansion YoY in Q2 2026 [Actual] |\n| Regulatory barriers | 2 | Stable | Cross-border tax/duty/de minimis complexity IS the moat; but tariff rules can change |\n| Data moat | 2 | Widening | Handles $8.9B GMV [guidance]; duty, fraud, and localization data improves conversion |\n| **TOTAL** | **14/21** | **Widening** | **WIDE MOAT** |\n\n**Step 2-3 Lynch Classification: Fast Grower** (sustained +28-40% revenue growth, Rule of 50 achieved, category share gains). Checkpoints: (1) revenue growth durability \u2014 supported by GMV +44% and multi-year merchant cohort onboarding [Actual]; (2) margin expansion \u2014 330bps in Q1, 300bps in Q2 2026 [Actual]; (3) balance sheet \u2014 net cash [Estimate].\n\n**Step 2-4 Financial Strength Scorecard:**\n\n| Metric | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue CAGR (5-yr, FY2020-25) | +47.8% | [Arithmetic on Filed] |\n| Last-4Q revenue growth | ~+33% | [Estimate \u2014 FY25 +28%, FY26 guided +38%] |\n| Gross margin (FY2025) | 45.3% | [Arithmetic on Filed: $436M/$962M] |\n| GAAP operating margin (FY2025) | 7.4% | [Arithmetic on Filed] |\n| Adjusted EBITDA margin (Q2 2026) | 20.9% (+300bps YoY) | [Actual - company release] |\n| ROE (vendor) | 17.0% | [Aggregator] |\n| FCF (FY2025) | $281M | [Arithmetic on Filed: OCF $284M \u2212 capex $3M, pack notes add back SBC] |\n| SBC (FY2025) | $39M (4.1% of revenue) | [Filed] |\n| Net cash position | \u2248 +$250M | [Estimate] |\n| Working capital (FY2025) | $477M positive | [Filed] |\n\nFinancial Strength Judgment: **Excellent** \u2014 net cash, strong OCF (30% of revenue), minimal capex, improving GAAP profitability.\n\n**Step 2-5 Capital Allocation Scorecard:**\n\n| Criterion | Score | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Buyback efficiency | 2 | $68M executed Q2 2026; $500M authorized [Actual]; disciplined \u2014 below recent peak price $43.99 [Aggregator] |\n| M&A track record | 1 | Passport just closed; too early to score ROIC. Mix score reflects uncertainty. |\n| Capex efficiency | 3 | Capex < 0.5% of revenue; asset-light model; incremental ROIC extremely high |\n| Rationality of mix | 2 | Prioritizing growth + opportunistic buybacks; sensible |\n| Guidance accuracy | 3 | Raised guidance 2 of last 2 quarters [Actual]; Q2 beat across all metrics |\n| Insider ownership bonus | +1 | Insider ownership 30.53% [Aggregator] |\n| **TOTAL** | **12/15 + 1 bonus = 13/15** | **Excellent** |\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n\n**Step 2.5-1 R&D Capitalization:** R&D not broken out in pack [Unconfirmed - not held]. Platform companies of this scale typically run 15-20% of revenue R&D; capitalized and amortized over 4 years, adjusted operating income and invested capital both rise. I conservatively estimate muted impact \u2014 pass-through fulfillment limits R&D intensity. **No adjustment made** to avoid compounding an [Unconfirmed] input into the valuation.\n\n**Step 2.5-2 SBC Treatment:** SBC expensed as cash (deducted from FCF in my DCF). FY2025 SBC $39M [Filed]; 2026E $55M, rising to $110M by 2030 [Assumption \u2014 ~4% of revenue, consistent with 4.1% FY25]. Vendor adjusted EBITDA of $62.4M in Q2 2026 includes SBC add-back; my model treats SBC as a real economic cost. **Adjusted FCF = Reported FCF \u2212 SBC.**\n\n**Step 2.5-3 Operating Leases:** $24M [Filed] \u2014 capitalized but trivial. Adjusted net debt \u2248 +$250M net cash [Estimate].\n\n**Step 2.5-4 Brand/Data Assets:** GLBE's core asset is its duty/tax/shipping data across 100+ markets and $8.9B GMV \u2014 not on balance sheet. Not separately valued; it is the engine of margin expansion in my DCF.\n\n**Step 2.5-5 Adjusted ROIC:** [Unconfirmed] due to missing segment/R&D detail. Approximating NOPAT \u2248 $228M (FY26E adjusted) / invested capital \u2248 $1.0B incl. intangible adjustments \u2192 **ROIC \u2248 23% [Estimate]**, > WACC of 10.3%.\n\n**Step 2.5-6 Owner Earnings (FY2025):** Net income $68M + D&A $2M \u2212 maintenance capex ~$3M \u2212 \u0394WC ~$102M inflow (release of cash) \u2248 **$169M [Estimate]** \u2014 strong cash-generation quality; accent on \"release of cash\" in FY2025 (working capital was additive that year).\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 3 (HYBRID DCF + SEGMENT CROSS-CHECK, TIERED WITH ENGINE 1)\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n\n**3-A. Discount Rate Derivation:**\n\n| Component | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Risk-free rate (10Y UST) | 4.65% | [Actual - yCharts 24-Aug-2026] |\n| Equity risk premium | 4.9% | [Assumption \u2014 4.5-5.5% range typical at current rates] |\n| Beta | 1.15 | [Assumption \u2014 vendor reports 1.011; adjusted upward for Israel geopolitical risk, small-cap, consumer-cyclical exposure] |\n| Cost of equity | 4.65% + 1.15 \u00d7 4.9% = **10.3%** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Cost of debt | n/a \u2014 net cash | |\n| WACC | **10.3%** (range 9.5%-11.0%) | [Assumption] |\n\n**3-B. Explicit Forecast \u2014 Base Case:**\n\n| FY | Revenue | Growth | Adj. EBITDA Margin | Adj. EBITDA | D&A | SBC | Cash Tax Rate | Cash Taxes | \u0394WC | Capex | UFCF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | $1,330M | +38% | 21.7% | $289M | $6M | $55M | 15% | $34M | \u2212$25M | $5M | **$170M** |\n| 2027E | $1,702M | +28% | 23.5% | $400M | $8M | $70M | 16% | $52M | \u2212$30M | $8M | **$240M** |\n| 2028E | $2,076M | +22% | 25.5% | $529M | $10M | $85M | 17% | $74M | \u2212$35M | $10M | **$325M** |\n| 2029E | $2,429M | +17% | 27.0% | $656M | $12M | $100M | 18% | $98M | \u2212$30M | $12M | **$416M** |\n| 2030E | $2,745M | +13% | 28.5% | $782M | $15M | $110M | 18% | $118M | \u2212$20M | $15M | **$519M** |\n\n**Driver sourcing:**\n- **Revenue growth 2026:** +38% is [Actual \u2014 company guidance midpoint]. **2027-2030:** deceleration from +38% to +13% is **[Assumption, deliberately not spun into a hero story]**. Consensus forward growth for GLBE on yfinance is +27.5% revenue [Estimate \u2014 yfinance consensus], which I interpret as a 2027E figure; my +28% 2027E matches. Beyond 2027 no sell-side number exists in this pack \u2014 I assume fade-to-13% (2030) at a slope consistent with e-commerce platform maturation, which is a 22% CAGR over 2026-2030, near the top of the \"Rule of 50\" feasible trajectory.\n- **EBITDA margin 2026:** 21.7% [Actual \u2014 guided $278-300M / $1,305-1,355M]. **2027-2030:** 23.5% \u2192 28.5% **[Assumption]**. Evidence: Q1 2026 margin 19.9% (+330bps YoY), Q2 2026 20.9% (+300bps YoY) [Actual]; company cites AI-driven efficiency [Actual]. A 300bps/year expansion path from 20.9% would reach ~30% by 2028-29; my path (to 28.5% by 2030) is deliberately below the straight-line trend \u2014 conservatism against Fulfillment mix dilution.\n- **Capex:** 3-yr avg $2M [Actual], modeled at 0.3% of revenue **[Assumption \u2014 asset-light platform model]**.\n- **D&A:** FY25 $2M [Actual] \u2192 $15M by 2030 **[Assumption \u2014 includes Passport intangible amortization]**.\n- **SBC:** $39M FY25 [Actual] \u2192 $110M by 2030 **[Assumption \u2014 ~4% of revenue, flat mix]**.\n- **Cash tax rate:** 15-18% **[Assumption]** \u2014 company is Israel-based with substantial NOLs; pack confirms identity holds but does not disclose the effective rate. Q2 2026 GAAP net income $47.7M on $299M revenue [Actual] implies single-digit GAAP tax rate currently.\n- **Working capital:** \u0394WC modeled as \u22121.5% to \u22120.7% of revenue **[Assumption]** \u2014 caution: the pack's WC column is contaminated by cash swings (IPO proceeds and subsequent spend); I therefore model a modest operating WC drag. Fulfillment pass-through can create swings but tends to be self-liquidating.\n\n**3-C. Terminal Value & DCF:**\n\n| Component | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Terminal growth | 4.5% [Assumption] |\n| Terminal FCF (2030 \u00d7 1.045) | $542M |\n| Terminal value (WACC 10.3% \u2212 g 4.5%) | $9.35B |\n| #N/A PV of explicit FCFs (5y) | $1.19B |\n| PV of terminal value | $5.73B |\n| **Enterprise value** | **$6.92B** |\n| + Net cash | +$0.25B [Estimate] |\n| \u2212 Diluted shares | 177M [Estimate] |\n| **Intrinsic value per share (Base Case)** | **$40.51** |\n\n**3-D. Segment Value Cross-Check (Engine 3):**\n\n| Segment | 2027E Revenue | Multiple | Segment Value |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Service fees (platform, ~47%) | $800M | 8.0\u00d7 EV/Sales [Assumption \u2014 Shopify 8-12\u00d7, Adyen 8-10\u00d7] | $6.4B |\n| Fulfillment (logistics, ~53%) | $902M | 1.5\u00d7 EV/Sales [Assumption \u2014 logistics comps] | $1.35B |\n| **Total EV** | | | **$7.75B** |\n| + Net cash | | | $0.25B |\n| **Equity value / share** | | | **$45.0** |\n\nThe two engines bracket the valuation: **DCF $40.5 vs Segment $45.0 \u2192 central intrinsic value \u2248 $41-45.**\n\n**3-E. Reverse DCF (what the market implies):**\nCurrent price $40.55 \u00d7 177M shares = $7.18B equity, less $0.25B net cash = $6.93B EV. At a 10.3% discount rate, the market today prices for: FY2026-30 revenue CAGR of ~22%, 2030 adjusted EBITDA margin of ~28%, and 4.5% terminal growth \u2014 **precisely the central case of my model**. The market is not careless here.\n\n**3-F. Tornado Sensitivity (\u00b11\u03c3 key variables):**\n\n| Variable | \u22121\u03c3 | +1\u03c3 | IV Impact | #1 Driver |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Term. EBITDA margin (28.5% \u00b1 3.5pts) | 25.0% | 32.0% | $40.5 \u2192 $33 / $49 | **#1 \u2014 Thesis KPI: EBITDA margin %** |\n| 2027-2030 revenue CAGR (22% \u00b1 5pts) | 17% | 27% | $40.5 \u2192 $33 / $49 | **#2 \u2014 Thesis KPI: GMV & revenue growth** |\n| WACC (10.3% \u00b1 0.7pt) | 9.6% | 11.0% | $40.5 \u2192 $46 / $36 | #3 \u2014 Macro/rate sensitivity |\n| Terminal growth (4.5% \u00b1 0.5pt) | 4.0% | 5.0% | $40.5 \u2192 $38 / $43 | #4 |\n| Cash tax rate (\u00b1 3pts) | 15% | 21% | minor | #5 |\n\n**Top 3 Thesis KPIs:** (1) Adjusted EBITDA margin trajectory; (2) GMV/revenue growth retention; (3) Take-rate stability.\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n\n**Step 3.5-1 Competitive Response:** If GLBE succeeds, Shopify (its distribution partner, largest platform) and Adyen/PayPal will respond. Shopify has historically built in-house before partnering (Markets Pro \u2192 Managed Markets); the risk of a build-in-house move is the #1 competitive overhang. Score: **\u22122 (threat, but partnership is currently deepening \u2014 \"Managed Markets 2.0 expansion\" [Actual])**.\n\n**Step 3.5-2 Reflexivity:** Positive cycle intact \u2014 rising stock price \u2192 equity-funded M&A (Passport $175M stock consideration [Actual]) \u2192 larger logistics moat \u2192 more merchants \u2192 GMV growth. Negative cycle would only bite below ~$25 (would impair M&A currency and talent retention). Currently in the positive zone.\n\n**Step 3.5-3 Customer Behavior:** Early-adopter merchants (large global D2C brands) \u2192 mainstream (SMBs via Shopify Managed Markets) \u2192 late adopters. GLBE's 2025 merchant cohort is \"strongly performing\" per mgmt [Actual]; as penetration rises, LTV/CAC should improve if churn stays <10% \u2014 churn data is [Unconfirmed].\n\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\nSECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u250