onal 67.6% / insider 30.5% [Actual] \u2192 high insider alignment; thin\n  float \u2192 squeeze potential, but also future supply if insiders diversify\n\u2022 Options/sentiment: not retrieved [Unconfirmed]\n\u2022 Price $40.55 vs 52-wk $26.84\u2013$43.99 \u2192 near high; positive momentum post beat\n\u2022 Analyst PTs: low $41 / mean $50.15 / median $48 / high $64 [Aggregator] \u2014\n  sell-side uniformly bullish; note low PT $41 = only +1% from T0\n\u2022 Crowding risk score: **8/15** (momentum + institutional-heavy + consensus\n  upside) \u2192 reduce max weight \u22121pt (cap 4% not 5%)\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nGLBE adds idiosyncratic cross-border/tariff exposure with beta ~1.0. In a growth-\ntilted book it duplicates: (a) long-duration rate sensitivity, (b) consumer\ndiscretionary, (c) USD/trade-policy exposure. It diversifies payments/fintech\n(Adyen/Shopify) via its \"picks-and-shovels + regulatory\" profile. Net: modest\nadditive; cap at 4% given crowding and correlation with Shopify position.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n\nEdge at T0 = EV/price \u2212 1 = 36.67/40.55 \u2212 1 = **\u22129.6% \u2192 Kelly f \u2264 0 \u2192 no position.**\nAt $30: edge \u2248 +19% \u2192 half-Kelly \u2248 3\u20134% (bounded by conviction cap 4%).\nAt $25: edge \u2248 +35% \u2192 half-Kelly \u2248 4% (cap binds). Layer-5 vs Layer-6.5 gap at\nT0 is ~2pts (0\u20132% vs 0%) < 20pts \u2192 no re-analysis trigger.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nRisks: Shopify internalization (\u2212high); tariff/de-minimis policy shocks; fuel/\ncarrier surcharge margin compression (Q2 GM \u2212120bp [Actual]); SBC dilution if\nstock stagnates; Passport integration/earn-out; Israeli regulatory approval of\nbuyback [Actual \u2014 pending].\nCatalysts: Managed Markets v2.0 international expansion cadence; Passport\ncross-sell ($100M+ 2026 revenue [Actual]); duty-drawback scaling; buyback\nexecution; Q4 2026 seasonal strength (implied ~$467M, +39% [Estimate]).\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\nCommon bear triggers with typical portfolio: 10Y > 5% (de-rates all duration);\ntariff escalation on sub-$800 parcels (kills cross-border economics); USD\nstrength vs EUR/GBP (dampens inbound demand); consumer recession. Tail\ncorrelation ~0.8 with growth index in stress (2020/2022 pattern). CVaR: in a\n2022-style shock, 47x trailing P/E implies ~45\u201360% drawdown potential. Tail risk\nis material \u2192 supports the small position cap.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY)\n\nKPI triggers (violate \u2192 re-evaluate):\n1. GMV growth <25% YoY for 2 consecutive quarters (base path FY27 +27%)\n2. Adj EBITDA margin <19% (guide 21.7% [Actual]) \u2014 or GAAP op margin <10%\n3. Service-fee take rate erosion >50bp (stable [Actual])\n4. Shopify product announcements toward in-house cross-border \u2014 immediate red flag\n5. Gross margin <43% for 2 quarters (fuel/duty pass-through failure)\n6. SBC/revenue >5% sustained (kills GAAP margin pathway)\n7. Passport: 2026 revenue <$100M [Actual guide] \u2192 capital-allocation downgrade\n8. 10Y > 5.25% (WACC re-derivation) or Fed re-tightening\n\nPre-mortem (if this fails by 2031, why?):\nA. Shopify internalizes cross-border, Managed Markets volumes collapse \u2192 watch\n   Shopify product launches; early signal: GLBE share of Shopify GMV flattens.\nB. Tariff war II compresses cross-border demand and duty pass-through \u2192 early\n   signal: de-minimis threshold cut, GM <43%.\nC. Fulfillment margin squeeze + take-rate compression \u2192 early signal: GMV grows\n   but revenue/GMV <14.5%.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM (ADVERSARIAL)\n\nShort thesis (same data):\n1. 7.1x trailing / 4.7x fwd revenue and ~27x EV/(EBITDA\u2212SBC) \u2014 no margin of safety;\n   reverse DCF demands near-bull execution.\n2. Shopify is the customer relationship; \"Managed Markets\" is a dependency, not a\n   moat \u2014 the landlord can internalize the t